73|export const INSTRUCTIONS_PAYER_AGENTIC = INSTRUCTIONS_PAYER.replace(
74|  'You will receive a chart of dated entries, each headed by an id like note-012, then the claim, the plan\'s coverage criteria, numbered crit-1, crit-2, and so on, and the reason code the plan applied.',
75|  `You will receive an index of the chart, one line per entry with its id (like note-012), date, kind, and opening words, then the claim, the plan's coverage criteria, numbered crit-1, crit-2, and so on, and the reason code the plan applied. You do not have the entries themselves. Two tools fetch them: list_entries returns the index again, and read_entry returns the full text of one entry by id. Read every entry whose index line could bear on a criterion, and read any entry before you quote it: a quote must come from an entry you have read in full, copied exactly, and the verifier will refute a quote from an entry you only saw in the index. Most entries in a chart are routine traffic that does not bear on the claim; you do not need to read those. When you have read what you need, answer with the JSON object and nothing else.`,
