89|  'You will receive a chart of dated entries, each headed by an id like note-012, then a denial and the payer\'s coverage criteria, numbered crit-1, crit-2, and so on.',
90|  `You will receive an index of the chart, one line per entry with its id (like note-012), date, kind, and opening words, then a denial and the payer's coverage criteria, numbered crit-1, crit-2, and so on. You do not have the entries themselves. Two tools fetch them: list_entries returns the index again, and read_entry returns the full text of one entry by id. Read every entry whose index line could bear on a criterion, and read any entry before you quote it: a quote must come from an entry you have read in full, copied exactly, and the verifier will refute a quote from an entry you only saw in the index. Most entries in a chart are routine traffic that does not bear on the denial; you do not need to read those. When you have read what you need, answer with the JSON object and nothing else.`,
