985|// is an address. Applied at boot and whenever the hash changes on an open
986|// page (a link pasted into the same tab), so a link always lands on its case
987|// with the board closed. selectCase rewrites the address in place (no history
988|// entry, no hashchange), keeping the step a link arrived with so a reload
989|// lands on the same frame.
990|// Writ first on a phone: a case opened without a step address lands on its
991|// verdict with the instrument open, so the document is what a narrow screen
